      "scope": "target",
      "introducedIn": null,
      "suggestion": "In Curl.Networking.UnitLibrary, StreamConnection.ReadAsync rewrites every Windows read that fails with SocketError.ConnectionAborted as SocketError.ConnectionReset (ReportsAbortedReadAsReset). Narrow that rewrite to the case it was measured for: a peer that resets a connection it never half-closed (RST arriving just after the request). When the peer had already closed its side (FIN seen, as StreamConnection.HasPeerClosed detects) before Curl wrote the request, and the RST is the answer to that write, keep the WSAECONNABORTED so CurlSocketErrorText.ReceiveFailure prints curl's 'Recv failure: Connection was aborted'. For example, record HasPeerClosed in WriteAsync before writing, and skip the rewrite on the next failed read when it was true. Re-measure both shapes (upstream test1802's closed CONNECT tunnel, and BL-1450's reset-after-accept URLs) with Record-CurlExchange.ps1 before pinning, and add focused unit tests in Curl.Networking.UnitTests (StreamConnection) for both (ADR-0482). Explained by ADR-0419: the aborted-to-reset rewrite was decided for a reset right after accept; it does not cover a peer that closed before the request, where the Schannel curl prints 'aborted' in 9 of 11 runs; the ADR should be amended with the narrower rule.",
